Assembler Design
Supported Syntax
# Comments start with #
.text                    # Code section
.data                    # Data section (optional)

main:
    ADDI x10, x0, 256    # Scalar RISC-V
    VLOAD V1, 0(x10)     # NPU instruction
    BNE t0, x0, main     # Branch with label
Assembler Pipeline
Lexer: Tokenize into {LABEL, OPCODE, REGISTER, IMMEDIATE, ...}
Parser (Pass 1): Build symbol table (label → address)
Parser (Pass 2): Resolve labels, encode instructions
Output: Vector of 32-bit machine code
---

Supported Instructions
NPU Instructions (Opcode 0x77)
| Instruction | funct3 | funct7 | Operation |

|-------------|--------|--------|-----------|

| VLOAD | 111 | - | Vd = Mem[Rs1 + imm] |

| VSTORE | 111 | - | Mem[Rs1 + imm] = Vs |

| VLBC | 111 | 01 | Vd[0:3] = Mem[Rs1 + imm] (broadcast) |

| VADD | 000 | 0000000 | Vd = Vs1 + Vs2 |

| VMUL | 010 | 0000000 | Vd = Vs1 * Vs2 |

| VMAC | 011 | 0000000 | Vd += Vs1 * Vs2 |

| VRELU | 100 | 0000000 | Vd = max(0, Vs1) |

| VCLP | 101 | - | Vd = min(Vs1, imm) |

| VREDMAX | 110 | 0000000 | Rd = max(Vs1[0:3]) |

| VARGMAX | 110 | 0000001 | Rd = argmax(Vs1[0:3]) |

| VCLR | 000 | 0000001 | Vd = 0 |

RV32I Subset
| Category | Instructions |

|----------|--------------|

| Arithmetic | ADD, SUB, ADDI |

| Logic | AND, OR, XOR, ANDI, ORI, XORI |

| Shifts | SLL, SRL, SRA, SLLI, SRLI, SRAI |

| Compare | SLT, SLTU, SLTI, SLTIU |

| Memory | LW, SW |

| Branch | BEQ, BNE, BLT, BGE, BLTU, BGEU |

| Jump | JAL, JALR |

| Upper | LUI, AUIPC |

| System | NOP (ADDI x0, x0, 0), HALT (custom) |

